# scripts/opcount: `readerbench bench mapstream N` reads a Map of four
# keys N times from a json.Stream over the text in memory, on the
# prelude's Reader interface (JSON-CURSOR-ALLOC): each key the Map keeps
# is a copy (stdlib.md json 2 and 8). The control is hand Go:
# encoding/json into a map[string]int.
unit read
sizes 20000 120000
args bench mapstream {n}
control benchmarks/wirereaders/testdata/control
